      <section class="section" id="stages" aria-labelledby="stages-title">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-head reveal" style="--lane: var(--mint)">
            <p class="kicker">Stages</p>
            <h2 id="stages-title">From an issue to a pull request, one checked step at a time</h2>
            <p>
              Each stage writes a file, and Natamux checks it before the task moves on. Where you want a
              say, the task stops and waits for you.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-wrap reveal">
            <svg class="flow-svg" viewBox="0 30 1070 240" data-flow role="img" aria-label="Context, Spec, Plan, then Test spec and Implement side by side, then Review, Testing and Release. Spec and Review wait for your approval.">
              <defs>
                <linearGradient id="lit" x1="0" x2="1" y1="0" y2="0">
                  <stop offset="0" stop-color="#f2b544" /><stop offset="0.5" stop-color="#58d3a6" /><stop offset="1" stop-color="#7fa8ff" />
                </linearGradient>
              </defs>
              <g data-edges>
                <path class="edge" d="M110 150 H 150" />
                <path class="edge" d="M250 150 H 290" />
                <path class="edge" d="M390 150 H 420 C 450 150, 440 80, 470 80" />
                <path class="edge" d="M390 150 H 420 C 450 150, 440 220, 470 220" />
                <path class="edge" d="M600 80 C 630 80, 620 150, 650 150 H 680" />
                <path class="edge" d="M600 220 C 630 220, 620 150, 650 150 H 680" />
                <path class="edge" d="M780 150 H 820" />
                <path class="edge" d="M920 150 H 960" />
              </g>
              <path class="edge-lit" data-path2 d="M390 150 H 420 C 450 150, 440 220, 470 220 H 600 C 630 220, 620 150, 650 150 H 680" />
              <path class="edge-lit" data-path d="M10 150 H 110 M 110 150 H 150 M 150 150 H 250 M 250 150 H 290 M 290 150 H 390 M 390 150 H 420 C 450 150, 440 80, 470 80 H 600 C 630 80, 620 150, 650 150 H 680 H 780 H 820 H 920 H 960 H 1060" />
              <circle class="token" r="6" cx="10" cy="150" data-token />
              <circle class="token" r="6" cx="10" cy="150" data-token2 opacity="0" />
              <g class="node" data-node="0" transform="translate(10 120)"><rect width="100" height="60" rx="12" /><text x="50" y="28" text-anchor="middle">Context</text><text class="sub" x="50" y="46" text-anchor="middle">context.md</text></g>
              <g class="node" data-node="1" data-gate transform="translate(150 120)"><rect width="100" height="60" rx="12" /><text x="50" y="28" text-anchor="middle">Spec</text><text class="sub" x="50" y="46" text-anchor="middle">spec.md</text><text class="gate-tag" x="50" y="-10" text-anchor="middle">waits for you</text></g>
              <g class="node" data-node="2" transform="translate(290 120)"><rect width="100" height="60" rx="12" /><text x="50" y="28" text-anchor="middle">Plan</text><text class="sub" x="50" y="46" text-anchor="middle">plan.md</text></g>
              <g class="node" data-node="3" transform="translate(470 50)"><rect width="130" height="60" rx="12" /><text x="65" y="28" text-anchor="middle">Test spec</text><text class="sub" x="65" y="46" text-anchor="middle">test-spec.md</text></g>
              <g class="node" data-node="3" transform="translate(470 190)"><rect width="130" height="60" rx="12" /><text x="65" y="28" text-anchor="middle">Implement</text><text class="sub" x="65" y="46" text-anchor="middle">code and tests</text></g>
              <g class="node" data-node="4" data-gate transform="translate(680 120)"><rect width="100" height="60" rx="12" /><text x="50" y="28" text-anchor="middle">Review</text><text class="sub" x="50" y="46" text-anchor="middle">the diff</text><text class="gate-tag" x="50" y="-10" text-anchor="middle">waits for you</text></g>
              <g class="node" data-node="5" transform="translate(820 120)"><rect width="100" height="60" rx="12" /><text x="50" y="28" text-anchor="middle">Testing</text><text class="sub" x="50" y="46" text-anchor="middle">tests pass</text></g>
              <g class="node" data-node="6" transform="translate(960 120)"><rect width="100" height="60" rx="12" /><text x="50" y="28" text-anchor="middle">Release</text><text class="sub" x="50" y="46" text-anchor="middle">pull request</text></g>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-notes reveal">
            <div>
              <h3>Side by side</h3>
              <p>Test spec and Implement run at once, each with its own agent. Release waits for both.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Checked, not trusted</h3>
              <p>A stage ends when its file has the right sections, the worktree is clean or your test command passes.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Run a stage as a workflow</h3>
              <p>For a hard Plan or Implement, Claude Code can run the stage as a workflow: more accurate, more tokens.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="cli" aria-labelledby="cli-title">
        <div class="wrap cli">
          <div class="section-head reveal" style="--lane: var(--sky)">
            <p class="kicker">Command line</p>
            <h2 id="cli-title">One command for you and your agents</h2>
            <p><code>natamux</code>, or <code>nmx</code> for short. Create and start tasks from your shell. Agents use the same command to say they are done or have a question.</p>
            <dl>
              <dt><code>task create</code></dt><dd>A new task, with notes, files or a GitHub issue</dd>
              <dt><code>agent start</code></dt><dd>A worktree, a branch and an agent in one step</dd>
              <dt><code>ask</code> / <code>done</code></dt><dd>What agents run to report back</dd>
              <dt><code>stage approve</code></dt><dd>Approve or send back without the window</dd>
            </dl>
          </div>
          <div class="mac reveal" role="img" aria-label="A terminal: nmx creates a task, starts Codex on it and lists the tasks.">
            <div class="mac-bar"><div class="lights"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><span>~/code/shop</span></div>
            <pre data-cli></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="more-title">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-head reveal" style="--lane: var(--amber)">
            <p class="kicker">And more</p>
            <h2 id="more-title">Small things that keep many agents calm</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="bento">
            <article class="tile wide reveal">
              <h3>A worktree per task</h3>
              <p>Own branch, own folder, own shells and ports. Your main checkout stays clean.</p>
              <div class="vis tree">
                <div><b>.natamux/worktrees/</b></div>
                <div>├─ <span class="a">T-0012</span>  natamux/t-0012-command-palette</div>
                <div>├─ <span class="m">T-0013</span>  natamux/t-0013-drag-tasks</div>
                <div>└─ <span class="s">T-0014</span>  natamux/t-0014-fix-token-refresh</div>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="tile wide reveal">
              <h3>It knows what each agent does</h3>
              <p>Natamux adds hooks to every session it starts: working, asking, waiting for a permission, done.</p>
              <div class="vis hookline" data-hooks>
                <span>session.start</span><span>tool.use</span><span>agent.asked</span><span>permission</span><span>stage.done</span>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="tile reveal">
              <h3>Attach files</h3>
              <p>Drop a spec, a log or a screenshot on a new task. Agents read it from the worktree.</p>
              <div class="vis files">
                <span><i style="--c: #7fa8ff"></i>design.pdf</span>
                <span><i style="--c: #58d3a6"></i>error.png</span>
                <span><i style="--c: #f2b544"></i>notes.md</span>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="tile reveal">
              <h3>Approval where you want it</h3>
              <p>Each stage can wait for you, or move on by itself.</p>
              <div class="vis">
                <div class="toggle-row"><span>Spec<small>Wait for my approval</small></span><span class="switch on"></span></div>
                <div class="toggle-row"><span>Implement<small>Moves on by itself</small></span><span class="switch"></span></div>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="tile reveal">
              <h3>Updates itself</h3>
              <p>The app checks GitHub, downloads in the background and verifies the checksum.</p>
              <div class="vis upd">
                <img src={`${base}icon.svg`} alt="" width="36" height="36" />
                <span>Natamux {version}<small>Ready to install</small></span>
                <span class="btn">Restart</span>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="tile full reveal">
              <h3>Your code stays on your machine</h3>
              <p>The daemon listens on 127.0.0.1 and asks for a token on every request. Your code goes only where your agents send it.</p>
              <div class="vis lock">
                <span>Account</span><span>Cloud server</span><span>Telemetry</span><span class="yes">MIT licensed</span><span class="yes">Runs on 127.0.0.1</span>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="tile reveal">
              <h3>Import issues</h3>
              <p>Turn GitHub issues into tasks. The issue becomes the context of the first stage.</p>
              <div class="vis tree"><div><span class="s">#142</span> Login redirect loops</div><div><span class="s">#139</span> Export as CSV</div></div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="section-head reveal" style="--lane: var(--sky)">
            <p class="kicker">Install</p>
            <h2 id="install-title">Up in two minutes</h2>
            <p>You need git and at least one agent installed and logged in, such as <code>claude</code>.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="install">
            <div class="inst reveal">
              <h3>macOS (Apple silicon)</h3>
              <ol>
                <li><a href={mac}>Download Natamux</a> and drag it to Applications.</li>
                <li>Releases are not signed yet. Open it once, then <b>System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Open Anyway</b>. Or clear the download mark:</li>
              </ol>
              <div class="cmd"><code>xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Natamux.app</code><button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button></div>
            </div>
            <div class="inst reveal">
              <h3>From source</h3>
              <p>Run the daemon and the dashboard with Docker or in a codespace. The dashboard opens on port 5173. Intel Mac and Linux builds are paused; the last release with them is <a href={`${repo}/releases/tag/v0.1.2`}>v0.1.2</a>.</p>
              <div class="cmd"><code>git clone {repo} &amp;&amp; cd natamux &amp;&amp; scripts/dev.sh up</code><button type="button" data-copy>Copy</button></div>
              <p style="margin: 16px 0 0">Checksums and the CLI in your own shell: <a href={`${docs}getting-started/install/`}>the install guide</a>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

